===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|clearstory|clerstory}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|clerestory}}, probably from {{m|enm|clere|t=[[clear]]: light, lighted}} + {{m|enm|story|t=[[storey]]/[[story]]: level of a building}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|architecture}} The [[upper]] part of a [[wall]] containing [[window]]s to let in [[natural]] [[light]] to a [[building]], especially in the [[nave]], [[transept]] and [[choir]] of a [[church]] or [[cathedral]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1939|month=July|title=Overseas Railways: Baltic Island Railways|journal=Railway Magazine|page=49|text=On the Visby-Västerhejde Railway there is a steam car. [...] The upperworks consist of a short '''clerestory''' coach body with end platforms and the engine chimney protruding from the roof like a stovepipe.}}

